    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0550" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg470"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-01-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 7, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 473.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instruction, No.
                    500, of the 21st of November last, inclosing a copy of a letter from Mr. Thomas
                    Pledge, of Iowa, respecting the case of Mr. Edward J. Janse, I have the honor
                        <pb facs="0551" n="471" xml:id="pg471"/> to inclose a copy of a note from
                    Lord Lansdowne, dated the 3d instant, from which it appears that Mr. Janse was
                    released on parole on the 5th of October last and is reported to have returned
                    to America.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d461-a1.xml" xpointer="d461-a1"/>
